use bit:
    uint8 for 8 capacity buffers
    uint16 for 16 capacity buffers
    uint32 for 32 capacity buffers

buffer: sequencial, consolidate

buffers of data structs type

####################################################################################################
a: mcache, of n1 slab's size
b: mcache, of n2 slab's size
c: mcache, of n3 slab's size
d: mcache, of n4 slab's size
case 1
|__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__|
 ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^
 a1  a2  b1  c1  b2  b3  d1  a3  n

 mcache a needs to allocate page, and n is the start of the new page.
 Lets assume that I can deduce a3 start addres + page size.
 In this case my impl works, right?

 case 2
 |__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__|
  ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^
  a1  a2  b1  c1  b2  b3  d1  a3  b4  n
  In this case my impl works, right?

 In this case mcache a3 will check memory at start of next,
 wich is b4, concludes that is occupied and store new slabs at start address of n

 case 3
 |__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__|
  ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^
  a1  a2  b1  n  b2  b3  d1  a3  b4

 If c1 mcache slabs is release AND that page was returned to the
 memory manager, then a requests memory and n is returned.
 mcache a a1 will check b4 start will find that is occupied,
 so n address will be used for a4 slabs storage.
  In this case my impl works, right?

 case 4
 |__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__||__|
  ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^   ^
  a1  a2  b1  n  b2  b3  d1  a3

 Same case as case 3, only after a3 there is no memory that belongs to the
 slab allocator. If I find a way to check and have a result "occupied" or "not valid",
 then address of n will be used.
  In this case my impl works, right?

